# Survey – generated by the "question‑me" skill

## Round 1

```survey-json
{
  "round": 1,
  "generatedAt": "2026-11-19T12:48:18.000Z",
  "stage": "stage-1792362077711",
  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "q1",
      "type": "single",
      "text": "What should live in the separate docs repo?",
      "options": [
        "Everything Kainbain: task docs, plans, reports and Kainbain settings",
        "Only task docs: plans, reports and task history (project settings stay with the main project)",
        "Other – describe in Notes"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "showIf": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q2",
      "type": "single",
      "text": "When you import or create a project, how should the separate-docs option appear?",
      "options": [
        "A visible field on the main form (easy to find)",
        "Tucked under an 'Advanced' section (keeps the form simple)",
        "Only offered when importing an existing project, not when creating a new one"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "showIf": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q3",
      "type": "single",
      "text": "The docs repo will usually be private. How should Kainbain and its runners log in to it?",
      "options": [
        "Use the same login as the main project repo",
        "Let me enter separate login details just for the docs repo",
        "Other – describe in Notes"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "showIf": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q4",
      "type": "single",
      "text": "When a project already has Kainbain docs and you switch on a separate docs repo, what should happen to the existing docs?",
      "options": [
        "Move them into the separate repo automatically",
        "Leave old docs where they are; only new work goes to the separate repo",
        "Ask me each time"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "showIf": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q5",
      "type": "single",
      "text": "For stealth use at work: should the main shared repo stay completely free of Kainbain traces?",
      "options": [
        "Yes – nothing Kainbain-related in the main repo, not even a small settings file",
        "A tiny settings or pointer file in the main repo is fine",
        "Doesn't matter for the first version"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "showIf": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q6",
      "type": "single",
      "text": "Task work normally happens on working branches in the main repo, which teammates could see. Should those working branches also stay out of the shared main repo?",
      "options": [
        "Yes – keep working branches out of the shared repo too",
        "No – branches in the main repo are fine, only the docs need to be separate",
        "Not sure – recommend whatever is simplest"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "showIf": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q7",
      "type": "single",
      "text": "Should one docs repo be usable for several projects, or strictly one docs repo per project?",
      "options": [
        "One docs repo can hold docs for several projects",
        "One docs repo per project only (simpler, keeps things separate)"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "showIf": null
    }
  ],
  "answers": {
    "q1": {
      "selected": [
        "Everything Kainbain: task docs, plans, reports and Kainbain settings"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    },
    "q2": {
      "selected": [
        "Tucked under an 'Advanced' section (keeps the form simple)"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    },
    "q3": {
      "selected": [
        "Use the same login as the main project repo"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    },
    "q4": {
      "selected": [
        "Ask me each time"
      ],
      "notes": "Can trigger a migration of some kind"
    },
    "q5": {
      "selected": [
        "Yes – nothing Kainbain-related in the main repo, not even a small settings file"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    },
    "q6": {
      "selected": [
        "No – branches in the main repo are fine, only the docs need to be separate"
      ],
      "notes": "Branches and such are fine just need to make sure we don't commit any files to main/master on the main"
    },
    "q7": {
      "selected": [
        "One docs repo per project only (simpler, keeps things separate)"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    }
  }
}
```

