1|#!/usr/bin/env node
2|/***
3| * MARK: run-tests.mjs
4| * @description Cross-platform full-project verification gate: the same seven
5| *   checks the old `run-tests.sh` ran plus the Container Tests branch, the
6| *   Frontend Build branch (exercises the deprecation gate), the Dependency
7| *   Audit Gate, the Proof Hygiene branch, and the Binary Guard branch, in a
8| *   single overlap window
9| *   (the two unit suites
10| *   alone take ~2x35s sequentially, so overlapping keeps the wall near one
11| *   suite), with identical `Running <name>... PASS/FAIL (<s>s)` lines and exit semantics —
12| *   but driven by Node (`node:child_process`, no shell), so it runs on
13| *   Linux, macOS, and Windows with only Node + npm installed. Shells out
14| *   only to `npm`/Node/Docker; the two environment-conditional branches
15| *   report SKIP instead of failing when their runtime is absent (Security
16| *   Script Tests without `bash`, Container Tests without a Docker daemon).
17| *   The fast branches share one overlap window; the Canary Tests branch runs
18| *   alone afterwards (see splitGatePhases) — same suites, same exit
19| *   semantics, but the heaviest branch never shares CPUs with the unit
20| *   suites. Fail-fast is ON by default (see resolveFailFast): when the fast
21| *   phase fails, the gate writes its verdict (`verdict.json` plus one
22| *   untrimmed `<branch-slug>.full.log` per failed branch) under
23| *   `$KAINBAIN_TASK_DOCS/ci-fast-gate-<timestamp>/`, prints the
24| *   `KAINBAIN_FAST_GATE_RESULT` banner, and skips the serial canary phase
25| *   with an explicit SKIP line — so the failure surfaces seconds after the
26| *   fast phase instead of ~13 minutes later. Opt out with `--no-fail-fast`
27| *   or `KAINBAIN_NO_FAIL_FAST=1` (canary still runs after a red fast phase,
28| *   but the verdict still lands early). A green fast phase always runs
29| *   canary (the #KB-0417 parity requirement); deploy.sh --prod passes
30| *   `--no-canary` to its final-test-suite gate, so fail-fast changes
31| *   nothing there. Failure Details tails stay bounded (120 lines by
32| *   default, `KAINBAIN_FAILURE_TAIL_LINES` to tune) with a `Full log:`
33| *   pointer at the untrimmed file; the verdict pointers are printed at the
34| *   gate's head and tail so they survive the engine's head+tail excerpts.
35| *   The Container Tests branch runs the static Dockerfile/compose assertions
36| *   only; the minutes-long live image build/boot tests are opt-in via
37| *   `KAINBAIN_CONTAINER_TESTS=live` (direct suite run, not the gate).
38| *   The Canary Tests branch (serial Playwright suite on its own scratch
39| *   stack, ~7 min) is IN the default gate so `npm test` and
40| *   `deploy.sh --prod` run the exact same suites and regressions surface in
41| *   the earliest automated stage, not at the merge/deploy gate (the
42| *   #KB-0417 incident). Opt out with `--no-canary` or
43| *   `KAINBAIN_SKIP_CANARY=1` for fast sanity cycles; `deploy.sh --prod`
44| *   passes `--no-canary` to its `final-test-suite` gate and runs the canary
45| *   suite as its own blocking `canary-e2e` gate, so nothing runs twice.
46| *   Measured gate wall is ~60-70s without canary (the two unit suites alone
47| *   are ~160s of CPU work) and ~366-420s with canary (the serial Playwright
48| *   suite is minutes long), so CI stages running this gate need an explicit
49| *   `timeout` override well above the 60s engine default
50| *   (`config.ciTimeoutMs`) — this project's stage sets 1800s. While branches
51| *   run the gate emits `▸ started <name>` lines and a `⏳ still running: …`
52| *   tick every 30s (`KAINBAIN_GATE_PROGRESS_INTERVAL_MS`), so a slow branch
53| *   never blanks the output (see scripts/lib/run-parallel.mjs).
54| *   `run-tests.sh` is a thin shim over this file so `deploy.sh --prod` and
55| *   older docs keep working.
56| * @example `npm test` => thirteen PASS lines (twelve fast branches + Canary Tests), exit 0
57| * @example `npm test -- --no-canary` => twelve PASS lines, exit 0
58| ***/
